This project reimplements in Rust the inference protocol of basal
(https://github.com/rkinas/basal, Copyright 2026 Remigiusz Kinas, Apache License 2.0) and ports parts of it:
the prompt format and letter readout (basal/prompt.py), the System One request handling and answer semantics
including multi, act, tool and set objectives (basal/server.py), facts injection (basal/facts.py -> crates/basal-core/src/facts.rs),
evidence spans (basal/evidence.py -> crates/basal-core/src/evidence.rs), shared-prefix packing (basal/engine.py),
and the experimental task layer (basal/tasks.py -> crates/basal-core/src/tasks/).
Reference requests in tools/reference include examples from basal/examples.

The basal model weights (Remek/basal-1.0-*, Remek/basal-1.5-*, Remek/basal-2.0-*, Remek/basal-omni-1.0-*) are not part of this repository; they are released by
their author under the Apache License 2.0.

Native Gemma 4 decoders and media processors/encoders follow Hugging Face Transformers 5.17.0
(https://github.com/huggingface/transformers, Copyright Hugging Face, Apache License 2.0).
The port also follows PyTorch antialiased bicubic resampling (PyTorch contributors, BSD-3-Clause).
The copyright notices, redistribution conditions and disclaimer are reproduced in licenses/PYTORCH-BSD.txt.

